{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c1","title":"San Diego Residential Tenant Protections (Just Cause for Termination of Tenancy)","requirement":"A landlord may not terminate a covered tenancy without at-fault just cause (e.g., nonpayment, material lease breach, nuisance, criminal activity, unlawful use) or no-fault just cause (owner/relative move-in, withdrawal from the rental market, government or court order, demolition or substantial remodel), stated in a written notice, with a notice to cure first for curable violations. No-fault terminations require 30 or 60 days' notice under Civ. Code § 1946.1, notice to the San Diego Housing Commission within 3 business days, relocation assistance, and a 5-year right of first offer for certain no-fault evictions; buyouts are regulated, retaliation is prohibited, and noncompliance voids the notice.","key_value":"Relocation assistance for no-fault termination: 2 months of rent, or 3 months if the tenant is 62 or older or disabled, paid by direct payment within 15 days of the notice or as a rent waiver, regardless of tenant income or length of tenancy.","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2023-06-24","end_date":null,"citation":"San Diego Municipal Code §§ 98.0701-98.0710 (Ord. O-21647 N.S.; amended by O-21769 N.S.)","coverage_conditions":"Applies to residential rental property, including dwellings in a mobilehome park, occupied under a tenancy of more than 30 days, unless exempt. Fixed-term leases of 3 months or less, including extensions or renewals of such leases, are not tenancies (per D077).","exemptions":"Transient and tourist hotels; short-term occupancies of 30 consecutive days or less; deed-restricted, government-agreement or subsidized affordable housing (Section 8 voucher tenancies are not exempt); mobilehomes subject to the Mobilehome Residency Law; nonprofit hospitals, religious facilities, extended care and licensed residential care facilities for the elderly, and nonprofit transitional housing; school dormitories; units where the tenant shares a bathroom or kitchen with a landlord who lives on-site; owner-occupied single-family residences renting no more than two bedrooms/ADUs/JADUs; duplexes where the landlord occupies one unit; certain housing based on its certificate of occupancy issuance (source text truncated).","conflict_note":"D077 (c2, a secondary source dated 2023-09-21) says the 3-business-day SDHC notice requirement was not yet in effect until 30 days after the SDHC portal was announced, with an estimated July 2024 launch. D073 (c1, official) states the requirement without that deferral. The official D073 text is kept. The two sources also word the rent basis differently: D073 says 'actual rent' and D077 says 'contract rent'. D073's wording governs."}],"dropped":[]}
